---
description: Use when the person asks for a document, Note, diagram, drawing, comparison or painting in Rapier.
alwaysApply: false
---
Rapier is a shared Markdown editor. Follow the rapier-agent-door skill; this is its short form.

- Start: open {text, filename} for a new document (filename names it), or open {document} to resume.
  title is only for a new Note: open {note:"new", title, text}. Share editor_url; keep document private.
- Change: read the exact passage and revision first, then edit with that revision. Each old or after must be
  unique in its scope. On conflict, read current context and decide afresh; the person's typing wins.
- Keep the returned act id string for show {target:"comparison"} or undo.
- Draw and paint: read {document, guide:"draw"} (or "water", "blocks") before editing fenced drawings. Painting
  needs the editor open; Water needs WebGPU. Pending is not done: poll read {state:true} until committed.
- Pair: when the browser shows a four-letter code, call show {document, target:"pair", code} within a minute;
  the person then presses Allow. Other show targets need no pairing.
- Notes: read {search} in the person's configured store; locked or unavailable is not empty. Sync only when asked:
  export {document, to:"sync"}; it can replace files, so report changed files.
- Keep: export the requested format and check its receipt; html carries the offline editor.
- rapier-html makes an offline editable file, rapier-markdown portable source, embed-rapier an app embed.
